                    "Description" : {
                        "Id" : "outcome_0_1",
                        "Name" : "Retire",
                        "Details" : "{TGT_MW.Callsign} just continues to sit in their seat, refusing to look up or make eye contact.\r\n\r\nAfter a small eternity, {TGT_MW.SUBJ} finally speak, \"I have problems getting dressed. It takes me a long time to do some of the most menial things Commander. I'm a liability out there and I can't risk any of my teammates just because I can't face facts.\"\r\n\r\nDarius' jaw tightens, \"What are you saying {TGT_MW.SUBJ}?\"\r\n\r\nStaring you dead in the eye, \"It's over! I'm tendering my resignation effective immediately Commander.\"\r\n\r\n\"If that's how you feel then we will grant your request. Go to the Barracks and clear out your stuff and Darius will see you off at the nearest port.\"\r\n\r\nResting your hand on {TGT_MW.Det} shoulder, \"...but not before we throw you the mother of all retirement parties first!\" \r\n\r\nYou see a smile grow across the pilot's face as they get up to shake your hand.\r\n\r\n\"Thank you Commander for everything.\", as they fight to hold back the tears.\r\n\r\nThe party draws everyone from all around. It seems that {TGT_MW.Callsign} was more popular than {TGT_MW.SUBJ} let on. You know this was ultimately the right call because the only other option was their name on the Memorial Wall.",
